  "review_text": "This month featured seven graded stories, spread over six issues (<i>Strange Tales</i> with two, as always), yielding a final weighted average of [SPAN: severity=info; fontsize=large; fonttype=bold; text=x.xx],\n\n... last month's <b>5.74</b>.\n\n\nThis may seem surprising given the high-quality of both the <i>Journey Into Mystery</i> and <i>Amazing Spider-Man</i> offerings, but unfortunately they were paired with the equally-horrible <i>Tales to Astonish</i> and <i>Fantastic Four</i>.&nbsp; It was a very uneven month with great variation.\n\nHighlights of the month were the surprisingly good Thor and Spider-Man stories, neither of which featured main-line villains, so the plots on these and the characterization won the day.&nbsp; However, the Porcupine, Infant Terrible, and the Scarecrow were all lame as all get-out and really dragged the rest of them down!&nbsp; The Wizard's appearance didn't help matters either, though we finally saw a glimmer of hope for Dr. Strange at least.\n\n\n\n[DEVNOTE: *** SUMMARY_BEGIN ***\n*** THIS MONTH ***7 graded stories over 6 issues...TOTAL WEIGHT: 4.58 grade character issue    weight 8.5   asm       ASM #10  1.00 7.5   thor      JIM #101 0.50 4.0   strange   ST #118  0.33 2.5   giant     TTA #53  0.75 2.5   torch     ST #118  0.50 2.0   iron      TOS #51  0.50 1.5   ff        FF #24   1.004.19*** LAST MONTH ***9 graded stories over 8 issues...TOTAL WEIGHT: 6.83 grade character issue    weight 9.2   asm       ASM #9   1.00 6.5   xmen      XMEN #3  1.00 6.0   ff        FF #23   1.00 6.0   iron      TOS #50  0.50 5.5   aven      AVEN #3  1.25 5.5   thor      JIM #100 0.50 4.5   giant     TTA #52  0.75 1.8   torch     ST #117  0.50 1.8   strange   ST #117  0.335.74\n*** SUMMARY_END ***]",
  "letters_page": "[DEVNOTE: *** INTRODUCTION_BEGIN ***\nEnforcers | villain | Milestone: (first)\nFancy Dan | villain | Milestone: (first)\nFrederick Foswell | villain | Milestone: (first: as Big Man)\nMontana | villain | Milestone: (first)\nOx | villain | Milestone: (first)\nNotes | villain | first | Infant Terrible\nNotes | first | Wizard's Anti-Gravity Device\nNotes | villain | first | Possessors\nScarecrow | villain | Milestone: (first)\n*** INTRODUCTION_END ***]\n[DEVNOTE: *** HIGHLIGHTS_BEGIN ***]\n[HANG0] * Odin punishes Thor, Loki exploits it, Zarrko benefits, and the Avengers discover that \"none of your concern\" apparently means \"go home.\"\n[HANG0] * Porcupine weaponizes a Giant-Man fan club, kidnaps the Wasp, and accidentally initiates an unexpected breakthrough for Hank and Jan.\n[HANG0] * FIXME - write something\n[HANG0] * Reed Richards, the Infant Terrible, and Big Joe combine forces to answer the question nobody asked:&nbsp; how much random nonsense can fit into a single comic book?\n[HANG0] * The Wizard unveils his new anti-gravity device, but Johnny and Sue end up trapped in a plot that feels strangely familiar.\n[HANG0] * FIXME - write something\n[HANG0] * Iron Man battles the Scarecrow, Pepper and Happy steal the comic, and basic geography quietly leaves the room.\n[DEVNOTE: *** HIGHLIGHTS_END ***]",
  "ownership": "That brings us to the end of 1963, but looking ahead to next month:\n[HANG0] * the Avengers welcome the return of another Golden Age hero from the 1940s\n[HANG0] * Thor still has the Tomorrow Man to deal with\n[HANG0] * Giant-Man and the Wasp travel south to take on a new villain\n[HANG0] * Magneto rolls out the debut of a new \"brotherhood\"\n[HANG0] * Doc Ock makes a return\n[HANG0] * the Human Torch <i>also</i> meets a new opponent\n[HANG0] * and so does Doctor Strange, behind a mysterious veil\n[HANG0] * Iron Man has to face the new threat of:&nbsp; the Black Widow\n[HANG0] * and the Thing takes on the Hulk!\n\nIt looks like a busy month... but <i>first</i>, we have to do the 1963 Year-End Summary!"
